From 481e04f9a0787ba6565de16dc77360ec07847718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viacheslav Biriukov <v.v.biriukov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 19:24:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Adds first-class IPv6 and DHCPv6 support to Smee.

The network must provide a stable way for Tinkerbell to identify client MAC addresses.
 - Direct clients need an EUI-64-derived IPv6 source address.
 - Relayed clients should include DHCPv6 Option 79, alternatively, the relay peer address must be EUI-64-derived.

- `stateless`: replies with DHCPv6 stateless configuration and netboot data for clients with matching Hardware records. Address assignment is handled outside Tinkerbell by RA/SLAAC.
- `auto-stateless`: extends stateless mode for unknown clients, allowing default netboot responses and static fallback iPXE scripts without pre-created Hardware records. This mode is the DHCPv6 analogue of DHCPv4 `auto-proxy`.
- `reservation`: assigns the IPv6 address reserved on the matching Hardware interface through DHCPv6 `IA_NA` flows.
- `derived`: derives a temporary boot-time IPv6 address from the client MAC address and configured direct or relay prefixes when no IPv6 reservation exists.

Signed-off-by: Viacheslav Biriukov <v.v.biriukov@gmail.com>
